<b>Madonna - Bedtime Stories: Instrumentals (1994) <b><b>| </b></b>AAC 256kbps / 48kHz </b><br>
<br>
<i><b>Bedtime Stories</b></i> is the sixth studio album by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Americans" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">American</a> singer and songwriter <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madonna" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Madonna</a>, released on October 24, 1994, by <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maverick_(company)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Maverick</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sire_Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Sire Records</a>. In 1992, Madonna released her fifth studio album <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erotica_(album)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Erotica</a></i>, the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_table_book" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">coffee table book</a> <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sex_(book)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Sex</a></i>, and starred in the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erotic_thriller" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">erotic thriller</a> <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Body_of_Evidence_(1993_film)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Body of Evidence</a></i>. Due to their sexually explicit nature, all three projects were negatively received by critics and fans, who felt Madonna had "gone too far" and that her career was over. Madonna decided that she needed to soften her image if she wanted to regain her audience. The first attempt was the ballad "<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I'll_Remember" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">I'll Remember</a>" from the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/With_Honors_(film)#Soundtrack" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">soundtrack</a> to the 1994 film <i><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/With_Honors_(film)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">With Honors</a></i>, which received positive reviews and reached number two on the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow"><i>Billboard</i> Hot 100</a>.<br>
